# Community build profile.
#
# Run `yarn build:community` (vite build --mode community) for a build that a deployment can point
# at its own backend and identity provider after the build, without rebuilding. vite.config.ts
# loads .env.production first and this file on top, so it only needs the flag below: same code,
# same commit, no fork. Without the mode you get the default (ALA) build, with the flag off.
#
# See community/config.js for the keys a deployment can set.

# Keep <script src="/config.js"> and config.local.js in index.html and copy community/ to the output.
VITE_RUNTIME_CONFIG_ENABLED=true
